 ## Overview
-This method addresses the non-convex optimization problem inherent in reconstructing 3D density fields using non-monotonic transfer functions (TFs) in differentiable volume rendering. Standard density optimization with non-monotonic TFs (e.g., Gaussian) is prone to local minima where gradients point away from the true solution [S1][S2, unofficial]. The method solves this by decoupling the problem: it first optimizes a "color volume" storing RGB emission and scalar absorption directly, bypassing the TF-induced non-convexity, and then estimates a density field that matches this color volume to serve as a robust initialization for the final density optimization [S1][S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from direct density optimization by avoiding early convergence to incorrect local minima caused by poor initialization [S1].
